lican lean keep this competitive"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point Democratic: the district's R+3 lean is outweighed by a favorable midterm environment, Stelson's money advantage, and polls showing her narrowly ahead even from Republican-friendly pollsters. Markets price Stelson around 80-90%, and the expert consensus is a Democratic flip, though Inside Elections still calls it a tossup and incumbency gives Perry a floor.", "watch": "A late shift on the economy or the Iran war debate, or a polling error in either direction, could move this between tossup and likely-D territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Scott Perry (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Pennsylvania's 10th District pairs a slight Republican partisan lean with a Democratic-leaning national midterm environment, producing one of the cycle's most closely watched House races. Six-term incumbent Scott Perry faces a well-funded challenge from former TV anchor Janelle Stelson, who has out-raised him and holds a cash advantage. Recent polls, including one from a Republican-leaning pollster, show Stelson narrowly ahead, and most expert raters now forecast a Democratic flip, though one still rates the race a tossup.\n\nPrediction markets put Stelson's chances in the low-to-mid 80s. The race has stayed tight in tone, with heated debates in mid-October and a controversial Perry ad drawing attention. Perry's incumbency and the district's lean give him a path, but the weight of polling, money, and ratings favors Stelson by a modest margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7335, "margin": 3.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7265, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7615, "margin": 4.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7786, "margin": 4.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7238, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7163, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7699, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7923, "margin": 4.5},